    "id": "41dc8e6d7ec70d7813e09505a7261115fae11a39",
    "message": "Fix kubectl-plugin test's Windows script-path resolution for non-venv CI runners\n\nCI (just added in the prior commit) caught this on its very first run: both\nWindows jobs failed test_kubectl_plugin.py with FileNotFoundError.\n\n_venv_script_dir() used Path(sys.executable).parent, which only equals the\nconsole-scripts directory for a venv/virtualenv layout (python.exe and\nkai.exe are siblings in Scripts\\). GitHub's windows-latest runner installs\nPython directly via actions/setup-python with no venv, so console scripts\ninstalled by `pip install -e .` land in a separate Scripts\\ subdirectory one\nlevel below python.exe's own directory -- the old helper silently pointed at\nthe wrong directory, which only surfaced once a subprocess actually tried to\nrun kai.exe from it.\n\nSwitched to sysconfig.get_path(\"scripts\"), which resolves correctly for both\nlayouts on both platforms. Verified locally (still correct under this\nproject's own .venv) and the full suite still passes: 379 passed, 2 skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <redacted@example.invalid>",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-16T04:28:41Z",
    "tree_id": "54ef0ebc824bd545021c13f269afee8a65ff695a"
